  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tunisia  Institution Building for Debt and Budget Management</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This capacity-building program aims to upgrading debt and budget management functions, achieving the following goals:  &#xb7;   Introduce active debt management, by: (i) reorganizing sovereign debt management functions; (ii) adopting state-of the art risk management tools; and (iii) upgrading the government debt information system (SIADE) in order to improve its functionality and data security; &#xb7;   Formulate a medium-term expenditure framework. The proposed program will help strengthen fiscal management by: &#xb7;   introducing risk mitigation procedures for different types of public liabilities, thereby increasing the predictability of budgetary outflows; &#xb7;   increasing the accountability, transparency, and cost efficiency of public liability management by facilitating the consolidation of key debt management functions; &#xb7;   equipping the MOF with tools to reveal the true cost of government liabilities and policy commitments within a medium-term framework. none</narrative>
  </description>
